one concern, not a blocker: background location tracking + the scanner sdk are the two places we'll touch native code anyway. react native gives us a js bridge to maintain on both platforms for exactly the parts that matter most. fwiw i still think it's the right call - two native codebases with our headcount would be malpractice - but let's budget for the fact that maybe 15% of the app is still platform-specific. scanner sdk also needs a RN wrapper written, that's ravi's learning project imo.

